From 4a898cb7f12029132d372ff9d32e5e64440ef34a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ws07 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 00:13:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 12/15] Web client: no world end or reset in the page's words;
 the world's continuity and the war period said apart
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The project's direction is a world that does not end or reset with a
period, and a war period (戦期) that is a separate thing whose bounds,
tally and prizes are not decided. This program still has an end turn, so
the page now says it as what it is: the turn after which this program takes
no new order, an old-style season's. It never says this as the world
ending: the dial reads 受付終了, the join card's line and WrongStatus name
the program, and the conquest card says the conquest (an old-style season)
is over. The map's edge is "the map as it is now", the daily quota turns
with the game day, rings open as turns go on, and a different season record
is said as another record, not as the world starting over.

hud/worldclock.mjs defines no world and no period. It says, on separate
lines, what workstreams 04/08 register: that the world goes on, and the war
period in force with its tally or "not decided". With nothing registered it
says nothing of either. With continuity registered, the program's end turn
is not said and WrongStatus is not put down to it. Tests: the words checked
for world end and reset, the two lines apart, and the away summary's mark,
book and an arrival across a period's boundary and a restart, each record
told once. Applies after 0011.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
